~ citizen_madero

Citizen: Have you heard about Francisco I. Madero?

Citizen: He was a wealthy landowner who believed Mexico should have fair elections and democracy.

Citizen: In 1910, Madero called on the people to rise up against Porfirio Díaz.

- What did Madero want?
    Citizen: He wanted democratic reforms and free elections so the people could choose their leaders.
    => END

- Was Madero a soldier?
    Citizen: Not really. He was more of a political leader who inspired others to fight for change.
    => END

